# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# .gitignore  --  Football AI project
#
# GUIDING RULE: Git stores CODE and SMALL TEXT (docs, configs, notebooks).
# It must NOT store: large data, secrets, model binaries, caches, or anything
# that can be regenerated by running a script.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Secrets / credentials -------------------------------------------------
# API keys, DB passwords, tokens. If this ever leaks it is public forever.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
secrets.yaml
configs/secrets.yaml

# --- Data ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Raw datasets can be 100s of MB - GBs. They are downloaded by a script, so
# the script is the "source of truth", not the files. We keep the folders
# (via .gitkeep) but ignore their contents.
data/raw/*
data/interim/*
data/processed/*
data/external/*
!data/**/.gitkeep

# Common data file types, wherever they appear
*.csv
*.parquet
*.feather
*.json          # NOTE: StatsBomb data is JSON. If we ever need to commit a
                #       tiny sample JSON, force-add it: git add -f path.json
*.jsonl
*.xlsx
*.zip
*.tar.gz
*.7z
*.h5
*.hdf5
*.sqlite
*.db
*.duckdb

# --- Models / experiment tracking ---------------------------------------
# Trained model weights are large binaries and are reproducible from code +
# data + config + random seed. We version them with a model registry later,
# not Git.
models/*.pkl
models/*.joblib
models/*.pt
models/*.pth
models/*.onnx
*.ckpt
mlruns/
wandb/
lightning_logs/

# --- Python ------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
env/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# --- OS / editor -----------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

# --- Notebooks output (optional, discuss later) ----------------------
# We currently COMMIT notebook outputs so results are visible on GitHub.
# If diffs get noisy we will add nbstripout. Left here as a reminder.
